{"id":"word:hebrew:H4519","type":"word","title":"מְנַשֶּׁה","subtitle":"H4519 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"Menashsheh , a grandson of Jacob, also the tribe descended from him, and its territory","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to מְנַשֶּׁה (H4519) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-pr-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 146 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"מְנַשֶּׁה (Mᵉnashsheh) means Menashsheh , a grandson of Jacob, also the tribe descended from him, and its territory First listed occurrence: 1Chr 3 13."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"מְנַשֶּׁה","transliteration":"Mᵉnashsheh","pronunciation":"men-ash-sheh'","strong":"H4519","lemmaId":"hebrew:H4519","partOfSpeech":"n-pr-m","forms":["מְנַשֶּׁ֔ה","מְנַשֶּׁ֑ה","מְנַשֶּׁ֖ה","מְנַשֶּׁ֗ה","מְנַשֶּׁ֥ה"],"morphs":[["HNp",113],["HTd/Np",12],["HC/Np",11],["HR/Np",7],["HC/R/Np",3]]},"definitions":{"short":"Menashsheh , a grandson of Jacob, also the tribe descended from him, and its territory","usage":"Manasseh.","full":"H4519. Menashsheh מְנַשֶּׁה 136 proper name, masculine person and tribe Manasseh (interpretation of Gen 41:51 as Pi`el causative √II. נשׁה q. v.); &#8212; ׳מ 46:20 +; מְנַשֶּׁ֑ה 41:51 + (on Judg 18:30 see משֶׁה ); with article (strangely), ׳הַמְֿ Josh 1:12 10 t. (see below); ᵐ5 Μαν ( ν ) ασση ; — 1 a. Manasseh , eldest son of Joseph Gen 41:51 ; 48:1 , 13 , 14 (twice in verse); 48:17 , 20 (twice in verse), also 50:23 (father of Machir; all E), 46:20 ; 48:5 (both P). b. of tribe, often + Ephraim (see אֶפְרַיִם ): (I) the part west of Jordan: a. מ ׳בְּנֵי Josh 16:9 ; 17:2 a ( הַנּוֺתָרִים ׳בנימֿ ), 17:2 b; 17:6 ; 17:12 (all J E), 1Chr 7:29 ; 9:3 ( וּמ אֶפְרַיִם ׳בְּנֵי ; Josh 13:29 see below); β. ׳מ alone, 17:5 , 8 (twice in verse); 17:9 b; 17:11 , 17 ; Deut 34:2 ( וּמ אֶפְרַיִם ׳אֶרֶץ ; all J E), 2Chr 30:10 ( id. ), Josh 16:4 ; 17:7 ; 17:9 a; 17:10 (all P), also apparently Deut 33:17 (poem), Judg 1:27 ; 6:15 , 35 ; 7:23 ; Isa 9:20 (twice in verse); Psa 80:3 10 t. Chronicles; γ. מ ׳מַטֵּה 1Chr 6:55 ; מ מַטֵּה ׳חֲצִי Josh 21:6 , 25 ; 1Chr 12:32 (van d. H v. 12:31 ); מ חֲצִי מַטֵּה ׳מַחֲצִית 6:46 (but on text see Kit); מ מַטּוֺת ׳שְׁנֵי וְאֶפְרַיִם Josh 14:4 (P); δ. מ שֵׁבֶט ׳חֲצִי 1Chr 27:20 ; with article הַמְֿ ׳הַשֵּׁבֶט Josh 13:7 (D). (2) of Manasseh east of Jordan; α. מ ׳בְּנֵי 22:30-31 , (P); β. ׳מ alone, Judg 11:29 (distinctly of territory), 12:4 (but on text see GFM), Psa 60:9 = 108:9 ; הַמ ׳חֲצִי 1Chr 27:21 ; γ. מ ׳מַטֵּה Josh 17:1 a 20:8 (both P), 1Chr 6:47 ; מ מַטֵּה ׳חֲצִי Josh 22:1 (D), Num 34:14 ; Josh 21:5 , 27 (all P), 1Chr 6:56 ; מ ׳בְּנֵי מַטֵּה חֲצִי Josh 13:29 (P); δ. מ שֵׁבֶט ׳חֲצִי Deut 3:13 (D), Josh 13:29 ; 22:13 , 15 (all P), 1Chr 15:18 , 23 , 26 ; 12:38 (van d. H v. 12:37 ); מ שֵׁבֶט ׳חֲצִי בֶּןיֿוֺסֵף Num 32:33 (P); with article הַמְֿ שֵׁבֶט ׳חֲצִי Josh 1:12 ; 4:12 ; 12:6 ; 18:7 ; 22:1 , 7 (all D), 22:9-10 , 11 , 21 (all P). Here belong also (chiefly) references to ׳מ as father of Machir (compare Gen 50:23 above): Num 27:1 ; 32:39-40 , 36:1 ; Josh 13:31 ; 17:1 , 3 (all P), 1Chr 7:14 , 17 ; and of Jair Deut 3:14 (D), Num 32:41 (P), 1Kin 4:13 (compare יָאִיר מָכִיר, ). (3) of undivided tribe (never מ ׳שֵׁבֶט ): α. מ ׳בְּנֵי Num 1:34 ; 2:20 ; 7:54 ; 26:29 ; 36:12 (all P); β. ׳מ alone, 1:10 ; 26:28 , 34 ; 27:1 b (all P), Ezek 48:4-5 , γ. מ ׳מַטֵּה Num 1:35 ; 2:20 ; 13:11 , מ בְּנֵי ׳מַטֵּה 10:23 ; 34:13 (all P). 2 son of Hezekiah, and king of Judah (Assyrian Menasê, Minsê Schr COT 2Kin 21:1 ); — 20:21 ; 21:1 9 t. Kings, 12 t. Chronicles, Jer 15:4 . 3 two who had taken strange wives: a. Ezra 10:30 . b. Ezra 10:33 .","rootNote":"from 5382 ; causing to forget ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 3 13","keyReferences":["1Chr 3 13","1Chr 5 18","1Chr 5 23","1Chr 5 26","1Chr 6 46","1Chr 6 47","1Chr 6 55","1Chr 6 56"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"e